* Ref: ../dbase3-decomp/specs/commands/set-commands.md:165
* SET UNIQUE ON / INDEX ... UNIQUE; REINDEX keeps the index's own uniqueness
* (header flag) regardless of the SET UNIQUE state at REINDEX time.
? "[W2-BEGIN]"
USE BASE
GO 2
REPLACE CITY WITH "HONOLULU"
SET UNIQUE ON
INDEX ON CITY TO U1
SET UNIQUE OFF
INDEX ON CITY TO U2 UNIQUE
INDEX ON CITY TO U3
SET UNIQUE ON
INDEX ON CITY TO U4 UNIQUE
USE BASE INDEX U3
? "[NONUNIQUE REINDEX UNDER UNIQUE ON]"
REINDEX
LIST NAME, CITY
SET UNIQUE OFF
USE BASE INDEX U1
? "[UNIQUE REINDEX UNDER UNIQUE OFF]"
REINDEX
LIST NAME, CITY
USE BASE INDEX U2
? "[UNIQUE KEYWORD INDEX]"
LIST NAME, CITY
? "[W2-END]"
RETURN
